# device-layer-0024.
# The person's calendar: EventKit on macOS and iOS, the CalendarContract provider on Android. A browser has no calendar
# of the person's to reach, so it answers `unavailable`.
#
#   add-event(title, start, end)   `added <id>`, the platform's own identifier for the event, kept in the default
#                                  calendar for new events (on Android a local calendar of the app's own, made the
#                                  first time, when the device has none it can write). Or invalid (a time this cannot
#                                  read, or an end before the start)
#   find-events(from, to)          every event that overlaps the span, one a line: start, a tab, end, a tab, the title,
#                                  sorted by start and then title. Or none (no event in the span), or invalid
#   remove-event(id)               removed, or absent (no event has that identifier)
#
# Each also answers not-determined (ask first: request-permission calendar), denied, unavailable or failed. Write-only
# access, which iOS 17 and macOS 14 let a person give, reads `denied`: this module reads events as well as writing them.
#
# A time is ISO 8601 with its offset, `2030-01-01T09:00:00Z` or `2030-01-01T10:00:00+01:00`, and every time this
# answers is in UTC to the second, in the first form. A title holding a tab or a line break has it read as a space. An
# event that repeats is answered once for each time it falls in the span.
#
# A host with no such capability (the server, the memory host) answers `unavailable`. Every answer is text from the
# closed sets above, or the lines, so an app compares strings and no platform type ever reaches it.

load ./native/{platform}/calendar
  find write-event
  find read-events
  find delete-event

task add-event
  take title, like text
  take start, like text
  take end, like text
  like text
  send back
    call write-event
      read title
      read start
      read end

task find-events
  take from, like text
  take to, like text
  like text
  send back
    call read-events
      read from
      read to

task remove-event
  take id, like text
  like text
  send back
    call delete-event
      read id
